<http://data.silknow.org/object/1c97d81d-51b9-307b-81cb-b110a580bce1/observation/4>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "This white satin waistcoat is extravagantly trimmed with dyed rabbit fur. Occasionally used as a decorative trimming on men’s and women’s dress in the 18th century, it has been arranged in strips here to imitate fringing. The fur appears to have been dyed a rather acid green, although it is possible that the colour has undergone a chemical change. The waistcoat is also decorated with narrow black velvet ribbon, embroidered with silver foil, purl and glass paste."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/1c97d81d-51b9-307b-81cb-b110a580bce1> .

